{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Cold Wave Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the cold, heavy, droning lead of late-70s and early-80s cold wave and new wave: a wall of detuned saws an octave deep, a vibrato creeping in as the note holds.\n\nHow it's built: three oscillators on one note: two saws a few cents apart, a third an octave below. The Ladder filter takes off the top. The vibrato fades in (an LFO through a VCA opened by a slow envelope, into all three FM inputs). A gentle Chorus and a Reverb. One voice.\n\nPlay: slow, stark melodies, long notes.\n\nTweak: the second oscillator's TUNE, the filter's CUTOFF, the vibrato envelope's ATTACK, the octave oscillator's level (mixer 3).",
